  "generated_text": "1. **Calculate the distance from $B$ to $C$:**\n   - Using the Pythagorean theorem, we find the distance from $B$ to $C$:\n     \\[\n     BC = \\sqrt{AB^2 - AC^2} = \\sqrt{3250^2 - 3000^2} = \\sqrt{10562500 - 9000000} = \\sqrt{1562500} = 1250 \\text{ km}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total distance for the trip:**\n   - The total distance is the sum of the distances from $A$ to $B$, $B$ to $C$, and $C$ to $A$:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total distance} = AB + BC + CA = 3250 + 1250 + 3000 = 7500 \\text{ km}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   - The total distance Piravena travels for her complete trip is:\n     \\[\n     \\boxed{7500 \\text{ km}}\n     \\",
